  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Communities and Return Contribution to Return and Re-integration in Kosovo (as per UNSC Res.1244 (1999)) Phase V (RRK V)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EU-Return &amp; Reintegration in Kosovo (EU-RRK) Programme is part of a longer-term partnership between IOM Kosovo, the EU Office in Kosovo, and the Ministry for Communities &amp; Return to support the process of return and help returnees to re-integrate into society. The overall objective of the Programme is to contribute to a stable multi-ethnic society by enabling sustainable livelihoods &amp; durable integration for returnees, Displaced Persons in Region, Internally Displaced Persons &amp; Refugees who freely choose to return or integrate in the place of displacement into Kosovo society. The IOM&#x2019;s EU-RRK Programme is set to provide the rights-based &amp; sustainable return &amp; reintegration of minority IIDP, IDP, &amp; refugee families. As such it undertakes a set of actions to help non-majority communities to have a strong footing in the community of their return &amp; provide them with basic socio-economic support. IOM is providing the following assistance free of charge for their selected beneficiaries that are recommended to be enrolled in the programme through the process &amp; procedures in accordance with the steps outlined in Regulation 01/2018 on the Return of Displaced Persons &amp; Durable Solutions: Newly built or renovation of existing house, Harmonized assistance package &amp; Income Generation assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
